Package: linkmapper
Title: Point-and-Click Linkage Mapping and QTL Analysis
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ebenezer", "Ogoe", , "ebenezerogoe@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           comment = "Co-creator; wrote the 2026 package"),
    person("Michael", "Obeng", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Co-creator of Linkmapper (2022)"),
    person("Stephen", "Amoako", role = c("aut", "cph"),
           comment = "Co-creator of Linkmapper (2022)")
  )
Description: A 'shiny' application and a set of plain R functions for
    building genetic linkage maps and locating quantitative trait loci in
    F2 intercross, backcross and recombinant inbred line populations. It
    wraps 'onemap' (Margarido et al. 2007 <doi:10.1111/j.2007.0018-0661.02000.x>)
    for segregation tests, two-point analysis, grouping, ordering and map
    estimation, and 'qtl' (Broman et al. 2003
    <doi:10.1093/bioinformatics/btg112>) for interval mapping and composite
    interval mapping with permutation thresholds. Results can be exported
    as figures, tables, a self-contained HTML report and an R script that
    reproduces the analysis.
